+- **Cross-origin HTTP**: HTTP responses carry only `x-trace-id`; the service
+  emits no `Access-Control-Allow-*` headers. Browser HTTP calls must therefore
+  be same-origin via the nginx proxy (`NEXT_PUBLIC_SOCKET_URL=/`). Pointing
+  `NEXT_PUBLIC_SOCKET_URL` directly at the realtime origin in dev yields opaque
+  CORS failures. Socket.IO applies its own `allowedOrigins` allowlist on the
+  handshake (API-P3-002).
 
